// Chapter 2 — the trail and the temple. Shows skill checks, item-gated choices, an entry check,
// and branches that converge again.

=== trail.river
@title The River

The trail ends at a brown river, swollen with last night's rain. On the far bank, through the trees, you
can make out a stair of green stone.

* [Tie off the rope and cross carefully] (requires: player has rope) { player:xp += 25 } -> trail.far-bank
* [Swim for it] skill-check athletics dc 12
  success: -> trail.far-bank
  failure: { player:hp -= 3 } -> trail.swept
* [Let Tomas find a ford] skill-check guide survival dc 13
  success: -> trail.far-bank
  failure: { player:hp -= 1 } -> trail.swept

=== trail.swept
The current takes your legs out from under you. You claw your way onto the far bank a long way downstream,
coughing up river and dignity in equal measure.
{if player:hp < 8}
You are bleeding from a gash along your arm.
{/if}
-> trail.far-bank

=== trail.far-bank
Tomas squelches up the bank behind you and stares up at the stair.

> guide: Well, {player:first-name}. It's real.

-> temple.door

=== temple.door
@title The Sealed Door

{image("temple-door", "Moss-covered stairs lead to a sealed stone door carved with a spiral, a closed eye and a hand.")}

A door of a single slab blocks the top of the stair. Three glyphs are cut deep into it: a spiral, a closed
eye, a hand.

* [Close your eyes and press the hand] (requires: flag:knows-glyphs) { faction:explorers-guild += 5; player:xp += 50 } -> temple.hall
* [Force the door] skill-check athletics dc 14
  success: { set flag:door-damaged; faction:explorers-guild -= 10 } -> temple.hall
  failure: { player:hp -= 2 } -> temple.side
* [Look for another way in] -> temple.side

=== temple.side
Around the side of the temple, roots have pried open a gap between the stones. It's tight, dark and smells
of something old.

* [Squeeze through] { player:xp += 10 } -> temple.hall
* [Back to the temple door] -> temple.door

=== temple.hall
@title The Hall of Eyes

~ player:xp += 25

Your torch light slides over walls carved with thousands of eyes, all closed{if flag:door-damaged}, and
over the cracks your forcing left in the doorway{/if}.

::: skill-check perception dc 13
success: -> temple.niche
failure: -> temple.altar
:::

=== temple.niche
One of the eyes is open. Behind it, in a niche no bigger than your fist, sits a small idol of obsidian.

* [Take the idol] { give player idol; player:xp += 50 } -> temple.altar
* [Leave it be] -> temple.altar
